Along the Northern Wall of the Great Cavern~
   You are standing at the base of the northern wall of the great
cavern.  The wall vaults upward some thirty feet to a ceiling bristling
with stalactites, while of the stalagmites that once rose to meet them
only broken stumps and scattered fragments remain.  To the west and
northwest the cavern floor gives way to a pool of dark, murky water.
