The Winding Tunnel~
   The air here moves against your face, cool and smelling faintly of
open space, and somewhere ahead you can hear a hollow, echoing murmur
like wind across the mouth of a jug.  Coils of rope and a stack of rough
planks have been left against one wall.  The tunnel winds on to the east
and back down to the southwest.
